(window.DSA_TOPIC=window.DSA_TOPIC||{})["greedy"]={"id":"greedy","theory":"\n<h3>What it is</h3>\n<p>A <b>greedy</b> algorithm commits to the choice that looks best right now and never revisits it. It's only correct when you can argue an <b>exchange</b>: any optimal answer can be changed to include the greedy choice without getting worse. When that argument fails, the problem usually needs DP.</p>\n<h3>Interval problems</h3>\n<p>Intervals <code>[start, end]</code> almost always start with a sort:</p>\n<table>\n<tr><th>Goal</th><th>Sort by</th><th>Rule</th></tr>\n<tr><td>Merge overlapping</td><td>start</td><td>if <code>start ≤ last.end</code> extend, else open a new interval</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Max non-overlapping / min removals</td><td><b>end</b></td><td>keep the interval that finishes first, skip ones that overlap it</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Min arrows / points to hit all</td><td>end</td><td>shoot at the current end, skip everything it hits</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Max overlap at once (rooms, car pooling)</td><td>events (+1 at start, −1 at end)</td><td>sweep and track the running count</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Intersect two sorted lists</td><td>already sorted</td><td>two pointers, advance the one that ends first</td></tr>\n</table>\n<h3>Other greedy shapes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><b>Reach / jump</b> — track the furthest index reachable so far.</li>\n<li><b>Running balance</b> — gas station, valid parenthesis string: if the balance drops below zero, restart or adjust a range.</li>\n<li><b>Two passes</b> — candy: satisfy the left neighbour rule left→right, then the right rule right→left.</li>\n<li><b>Custom sort order</b> — largest number compares <code>a + b</code> vs <code>b + a</code>; two-city scheduling sorts by cost difference.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Template: merge intervals</h3>\n<pre><code class=\"py\">intervals.sort()\nout = [intervals[0]]\nfor s, e in intervals[1:]:\n    if s &lt;= out[-1][1]:\n        out[-1][1] = max(out[-1][1], e)   # overlap → extend\n    else:\n        out.append([s, e])                # gap → new interval</code></pre>\n<h3>Common mistakes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Sorting by start when the proof needs sorting by end (non-overlapping intervals, arrows).</li>\n<li>Off-by-one on touching intervals: does <code>[1, 2]</code> overlap <code>[2, 3]</code>? Read the problem — it differs between questions.</li>\n<li>Trusting a greedy without a counter-example check. Try a tiny tricky case by hand.</li>\n</ul>\n","qs":{"jump-game":{"statement":"<code>nums[i]</code> is the maximum jump length from index i. Can you reach the last index from index 0?","examples":[["nums = [2, 3, 1, 1, 4]","True"],["nums = [3, 2, 1, 0, 4]","False"]],"vizIn":"nums = [2, 3, 1, 1, 4]","brute":{"idea":"Recursively try every jump length from every index.","tc":"O(2ⁿ)","sc":"O(n)","code":"def can_jump(nums):\n    def go(i):\n        if i >= len(nums) - 1:\n            return True\n        return any(go(i + j) for j in range(1, nums[i] + 1))\n    return go(0)","setup":""},"opt":{"idea":"Track the furthest index reachable. If you stand beyond it, you're stuck; otherwise extend it with i + nums[i].","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(1)","code":"def can_jump(nums):\n    reach = 0\n    for i, x in enumerate(nums):\n        if i > reach:\n            return False\n        reach = max(reach, i + x)\n    return True","frames":[{"m":"From 0 we can reach up to 2","l":5,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"nums","v":["2","3","1","1","4"],"p":{"i":0},"hl":[0],"ok":[0,1,2],"bad":[]},{"k":"vars","v":[["reach","2"]]}]},{"m":"From 1 we can reach up to 4","l":5,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"nums","v":["2","3","1","1","4"],"p":{"i":1},"hl":[1],"ok":[0,1,2,3,4],"bad":[]},{"k":"vars","v":[["reach","4"]]}]},{"m":"From 2 we can reach up to 4","l":5,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"nums","v":["2","3","1","1","4"],"p":{"i":2},"hl":[2],"ok":[0,1,2,3,4],"bad":[]},{"k":"vars","v":[["reach","4"]]}]},{"m":"From 3 we can reach up to 4","l":5,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"nums","v":["2","3","1","1","4"],"p":{"i":3},"hl":[3],"ok":[0,1,2,3,4],"bad":[]},{"k":"vars","v":[["reach","4"]]}]},{"m":"From 4 we can reach up to 8","l":5,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"nums","v":["2","3","1","1","4"],"p":{"i":4},"hl":[4],"ok":[0,1,2,3,4],"bad":[]},{"k":"vars","v":[["reach","8"]]}]},{"m":"Result: True","l":-1,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"nums","v":["2","3","1","1","4"],"p":{"i":4},"hl":[4],"ok":[0,1,2,3,4],"bad":[]},{"k":"vars","v":[["reach","8"]]}]}],"setup":""},"tests":2,"ide":{"name":"can_jump","stub":"def can_jump(nums):\n    \"\"\"\n    nums[i] is the maximum jump length from index i. Can you reach the last\n    index from index 0?\n    \"\"\"\n    # Write your code here\n    pass\n","usage":"print(can_jump([2, 3, 1, 1, 4]))","tests":[{"args":"([2, 3, 1, 1, 4],)","want":"True"},{"args":"([3, 2, 1, 0, 4],)","want":"False"}],"listify":false,"design":false,"plain":false}},"jump-game-ii":{"statement":"Return the minimum number of jumps to reach the last index (it's always reachable).","examples":[["nums = [2, 3, 1, 1, 4]","2"],["nums = [2, 3, 0, 1, 4]","2"]],"vizIn":"nums = [2, 3, 1, 1, 2, 1, 4]","brute":{"idea":"dp[i] = 1 + min(dp[j]) over every j that can jump to i.","tc":"O(n²)","sc":"O(n)","code":"def jump(nums):\n    n = len(nums)\n    dp = [0] + [float(\"inf\")] * (n - 1)\n    for i in range(1, n):\n        for j in range(i):\n            if j + nums[j] >= i:\n                dp[i] = min(dp[i], dp[j] + 1)\n    return dp[-1]","setup":""},"opt":{"idea":"Treat each jump as a BFS layer: the current window [start, end] is reachable in k jumps; the furthest index reachable from it is the end of the next window.","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(1)","code":"def jump(nums):\n    jumps, end, far = 0, 0, 0\n    for i in range(len(nums) - 1):\n        far = max(far, i + nums[i])\n        if i == end:\n            jumps += 1\n            end = far\n    return jumps","frames":[{"m":"Window ends at 0: jump #1 lets us reach up to 2","l":5,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"nums","v":["2","3","1","1","2","1","4"],"p":{"i":0},"hl":[1,2],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"vars","v":[["jumps","1"]]}]},{"m":"Window ends at 2: jump #2 lets us reach up to 4","l":5,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"nums","v":["2","3","1","1","2","1","4"],"p":{"i":2},"hl":[3,4],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"vars","v":[["jumps","2"]]}]},{"m":"Window ends at 4: jump #3 lets us reach up to 6","l":5,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"nums","v":["2","3","1","1","2","1","4"],"p":{"i":4},"hl":[5,6],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"vars","v":[["jumps","3"]]}]},{"m":"Result: 3","l":-1,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"nums","v":["2","3","1","1","2","1","4"],"p":{"i":4},"hl":[5,6],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"vars","v":[["jumps","3"]]}]}],"setup":""},"tests":2,"ide":{"name":"jump","stub":"def jump(nums):\n    \"\"\"\n    Return the minimum number of jumps to reach the last index (it's always\n    reachable).\n    \"\"\"\n    # Write your code here\n    pass\n","usage":"print(jump([2, 3, 1, 1, 2, 1, 4]))","tests":[{"args":"([2, 3, 1, 1, 4],)","want":"2"},{"args":"([2, 3, 0, 1, 4],)","want":"2"}],"listify":false,"design":false,"plain":false}},"gas-station":{"statement":"Station i gives <code>gas[i]</code>; driving to the next costs <code>cost[i]</code>. Return the start index that completes the circle, or −1.","examples":[["gas = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5], cost = [3, 4, 5, 1, 2]","3"],["gas = [2, 3, 4], cost = [3, 4, 3]","-1"]],"vizIn":"gas = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5], cost = [3, 4, 5, 1, 2]","brute":{"idea":"Simulate the full loop from every start.","tc":"O(n²)","sc":"O(1)","code":"def can_complete_circuit(gas, cost):\n    n = len(gas)\n    for s in range(n):\n        tank = 0\n        for k in range(n):\n            i = (s + k) % n\n            tank += gas[i] - cost[i]\n            if tank < 0:\n                break\n        else:\n            return s\n    return -1","setup":""},"opt":{"idea":"If total gas &lt; total cost it's impossible. Otherwise drive once; when the tank goes negative at i, no station from the current start to i can work, so restart at i + 1.","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(1)","code":"def can_complete_circuit(gas, cost):\n    if sum(gas) < sum(cost):\n        return -1\n    start = tank = 0\n    for i in range(len(gas)):\n        tank += gas[i] - cost[i]\n        if tank < 0:\n            start, tank = i + 1, 0\n        else:\n            pass\n    return start","frames":[{"m":"Tank went negative at 0 → no start up to 0 works; restart at 1","l":7,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"gain = gas − cost","v":["-2","-2","-2","3","3"],"p":{"i":0},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[0]},{"k":"vars","v":[["tank","-2"]]}]},{"m":"Tank went negative at 1 → no start up to 1 works; restart at 2","l":7,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"gain = gas − cost","v":["-2","-2","-2","3","3"],"p":{"i":1},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[1]},{"k":"vars","v":[["tank","-2"]]}]},{"m":"Tank went negative at 2 → no start up to 2 works; restart at 3","l":7,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"gain = gas − cost","v":["-2","-2","-2","3","3"],"p":{"i":2},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[2]},{"k":"vars","v":[["tank","-2"]]}]},{"m":"Station 3: tank 3","l":9,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"gain = gas − cost","v":["-2","-2","-2","3","3"],"p":{"i":3},"hl":[],"ok":[3],"bad":[]},{"k":"vars","v":[["start","3"],["tank","3"]]}]},{"m":"Station 4: tank 6","l":9,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"gain = gas − cost","v":["-2","-2","-2","3","3"],"p":{"i":4},"hl":[],"ok":[3,4],"bad":[]},{"k":"vars","v":[["start","3"],["tank","6"]]}]},{"m":"Result: 3","l":-1,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"gain = gas − cost","v":["-2","-2","-2","3","3"],"p":{"i":4},"hl":[],"ok":[3,4],"bad":[]},{"k":"vars","v":[["start","3"],["tank","6"]]}]}],"setup":""},"tests":2,"ide":{"name":"can_complete_circuit","stub":"def can_complete_circuit(gas, cost):\n    \"\"\"\n    Station i gives gas[i]; driving to the next costs cost[i]. Return the start\n    index that completes the circle, or −1.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Write your code here\n    pass\n","usage":"print(can_complete_circuit([1, 2, 3, 4, 5], [3, 4, 5, 1, 2]))","tests":[{"args":"([1, 2, 3, 4, 5], [3, 4, 5, 1, 2])","want":"3"},{"args":"([2, 3, 4], [3, 4, 3])","want":"-1"}],"listify":false,"design":false,"plain":false}},"merge-intervals":{"statement":"Merge all overlapping intervals.","examples":[["intervals = [[1, 3], [2, 6], [8, 10], [15, 18]]","[[1, 6], [8, 10], [15, 18]]"],["intervals = [[1, 4], [4, 5]]","[[1, 5]]"]],"vizIn":"intervals = [[1, 3], [2, 6], [8, 10], [15, 18]]","brute":{"idea":"Repeatedly look for any two overlapping intervals and merge them until none overlap.","tc":"O(n³)","sc":"O(n)","code":"def merge_intervals(intervals):\n    res = [list(x) for x in intervals]\n    merged = True\n    while merged:\n        merged = False\n        for i in range(len(res)):\n            for j in range(i + 1, len(res)):\n                a, b = res[i], res[j]\n                if a[0] <= b[1] and b[0] <= a[1]:\n                    res[i] = [min(a[0], b[0]), max(a[1], b[1])]\n                    res.pop(j)\n                    merged = True\n                    break\n            if merged:\n                break\n    return sorted(res)","setup":""},"opt":{"idea":"Sort by start; extend the last merged interval while the next starts before it ends, otherwise start a new one.","tc":"O(n log n)","sc":"O(n)","code":"def merge_intervals(intervals):\n    intervals.sort()\n    out = [intervals[0][:]]\n    for s, e in intervals[1:]:\n        if s <= out[-1][1]:\n            out[-1][1] = max(out[-1][1], e)\n        else:\n            out.append([s, e])\n    return out","frames":[{"m":"Process [2,6]","l":7,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"sorted","v":["1-3","2-6","8-10","15-18"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"merged","v":["1-6"],"p":{},"hl":[0],"ok":[],"bad":[]}]},{"m":"Process [8,10]","l":7,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"sorted","v":["1-3","2-6","8-10","15-18"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"merged","v":["1-6","8-10"],"p":{},"hl":[1],"ok":[],"bad":[]}]},{"m":"Process [15,18]","l":7,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"sorted","v":["1-3","2-6","8-10","15-18"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"merged","v":["1-6","8-10","15-18"],"p":{},"hl":[2],"ok":[],"bad":[]}]},{"m":"Result: [[1, 6], [8, 10], [15, 18]]","l":-1,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"sorted","v":["1-3","2-6","8-10","15-18"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"merged","v":["1-6","8-10","15-18"],"p":{},"hl":[2],"ok":[],"bad":[]}]}],"setup":""},"tests":2,"ide":{"name":"merge_intervals","stub":"def merge_intervals(intervals):\n    \"\"\"\n    Merge all overlapping intervals.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Write your code here\n    pass\n","usage":"print(merge_intervals([[1, 3], [2, 6], [8, 10], [15, 18]]))","tests":[{"args":"([[1, 3], [2, 6], [8, 10], [15, 18]],)","want":"[[1, 6], [8, 10], [15, 18]]"},{"args":"([[1, 4], [4, 5]],)","want":"[[1, 5]]"}],"listify":false,"design":false,"plain":false}},"insert-interval":{"statement":"Insert <code>newInterval</code> into a sorted list of non-overlapping intervals, merging where needed.","examples":[["intervals = [[1, 3], [6, 9]], new_interval = [2, 5]","[[1, 5], [6, 9]]"],["intervals = [[1, 2], [3, 5], [6, 7], [8, 10], [12, 16]], new_interval = [4, 8]","[[1, 2], [3, 10], [12, 16]]"]],"vizIn":"intervals = [[1, 3], [6, 9]], new_interval = [2, 5]","brute":{"idea":"Append the new interval, sort everything, and run Merge Intervals.","tc":"O(n log n)","sc":"O(n)","code":"def insert(intervals, new_interval):\n    allv = sorted(intervals + [new_interval])\n    out = [allv[0]]\n    for s, e in allv[1:]:\n        if s <= out[-1][1]:\n            out[-1][1] = max(out[-1][1], e)\n        else:\n            out.append([s, e])\n    return out","setup":""},"opt":{"idea":"One pass: copy intervals ending before it, absorb every interval overlapping it into one, copy the rest.","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(n)","code":"def insert(intervals, new_interval):\n    s, e = new_interval\n    out, i, n = [], 0, len(intervals)\n    while i < n and intervals[i][1] < s:\n        out.append(intervals[i])\n        i += 1\n    while i < n and intervals[i][0] <= e:\n        s, e = min(s, intervals[i][0]), max(e, intervals[i][1])\n        i += 1\n    out.append([s, e])\n    out += intervals[i:]\n    return out","frames":[{"m":"1) Copy intervals that end before the new one starts","l":5,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"intervals","v":["1-3","6-9"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"out","v":[],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]}]},{"m":"2) Absorb [1,3] → [1,5]","l":7,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"intervals","v":["1-3","6-9"],"p":{"i":0},"hl":[0],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"vars","v":[["merged","[1,5]"]]}]},{"m":"3) Add the merged interval and copy the rest","l":10,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"out","v":["1-5","6-9"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[0],"bad":[]}]},{"m":"Result: [[1, 5], [6, 9]]","l":-1,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"out","v":["1-5","6-9"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[0],"bad":[]}]}],"setup":""},"tests":2,"ide":{"name":"insert","stub":"def insert(intervals, new_interval):\n    \"\"\"\n    Insert newInterval into a sorted list of non-overlapping intervals, merging\n    where needed.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Write your code here\n    pass\n","usage":"print(insert([[1, 3], [6, 9]], [2, 5]))","tests":[{"args":"([[1, 3], [6, 9]], [2, 5])","want":"[[1, 5], [6, 9]]"},{"args":"([[1, 2], [3, 5], [6, 7], [8, 10], [12, 16]], [4, 8])","want":"[[1, 2], [3, 10], [12, 16]]"}],"listify":false,"design":false,"plain":false}},"non-overlapping-intervals":{"statement":"Return the minimum number of intervals to remove so the rest don't overlap (touching ends are fine).","examples":[["intervals = [[1, 2], [2, 3], [3, 4], [1, 3]]","1"],["intervals = [[1, 2], [1, 2], [1, 2]]","2"],["intervals = [[1, 2], [2, 3]]","0"]],"vizIn":"intervals = [[1, 4], [2, 3], [3, 5], [4, 6], [5, 9]]","brute":{"idea":"Try every subset of intervals to keep and check it's non-overlapping.","tc":"O(n · 2ⁿ)","sc":"O(n)","code":"def erase_overlap_intervals(intervals):\n    n, best = len(intervals), 0\n    for mask in range(1 << n):\n        keep = sorted(intervals[i] for i in range(n) if mask >> i & 1)\n        if all(keep[k][1] <= keep[k + 1][0] for k in range(len(keep) - 1)):\n            best = max(best, len(keep))\n    return n - best","setup":""},"opt":{"idea":"Sort by end time. Keep an interval if it starts at or after the last kept end; otherwise remove it. Finishing earliest leaves the most room.","tc":"O(n log n)","sc":"O(1)","code":"def erase_overlap_intervals(intervals):\n    intervals.sort(key=lambda x: x[1])\n    end, removed, kept = float(\"-inf\"), 0, []\n    for i, (s, e) in enumerate(intervals):\n        if s >= end:\n            end = e\n            kept.append(i)\n        else:\n            removed += 1\n    return removed","frames":[{"m":"[2,3] keep","l":8,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"sorted by end","v":["2-3","1-4","3-5","4-6","5-9"],"p":{"i":0},"hl":[],"ok":[0],"bad":[]},{"k":"vars","v":[["removed","0"]]}]},{"m":"[1,4] overlaps → remove","l":8,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"sorted by end","v":["2-3","1-4","3-5","4-6","5-9"],"p":{"i":1},"hl":[],"ok":[0],"bad":[1]},{"k":"vars","v":[["removed","1"]]}]},{"m":"[3,5] keep","l":8,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"sorted by end","v":["2-3","1-4","3-5","4-6","5-9"],"p":{"i":2},"hl":[],"ok":[0,2],"bad":[1]},{"k":"vars","v":[["removed","1"]]}]},{"m":"[4,6] overlaps → remove","l":8,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"sorted by end","v":["2-3","1-4","3-5","4-6","5-9"],"p":{"i":3},"hl":[],"ok":[0,2],"bad":[1,3]},{"k":"vars","v":[["removed","2"]]}]},{"m":"[5,9] keep","l":8,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"sorted by end","v":["2-3","1-4","3-5","4-6","5-9"],"p":{"i":4},"hl":[],"ok":[0,2,4],"bad":[1,3]},{"k":"vars","v":[["removed","2"]]}]},{"m":"Result: 2","l":-1,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"sorted by end","v":["2-3","1-4","3-5","4-6","5-9"],"p":{"i":4},"hl":[],"ok":[0,2,4],"bad":[1,3]},{"k":"vars","v":[["removed","2"]]}]}],"setup":""},"tests":3,"ide":{"name":"erase_overlap_intervals","stub":"def erase_overlap_intervals(intervals):\n    \"\"\"\n    Return the minimum number of intervals to remove so the rest don't overlap\n    (touching ends are fine).\n    \"\"\"\n    # Write your code here\n    pass\n","usage":"print(erase_overlap_intervals([[1, 4], [2, 3], [3, 5], [4, 6], [5, 9]]))","tests":[{"args":"([[1, 2], [2, 3], [3, 4], [1, 3]],)","want":"1"},{"args":"([[1, 2], [1, 2], [1, 2]],)","want":"2"},{"args":"([[1, 2], [2, 3]],)","want":"0"}],"listify":false,"design":false,"plain":false}},"minimum-number-of-arrows-to-burst-balloons":{"statement":"Each balloon spans [x_start, x_end]. An arrow at x bursts every balloon with start ≤ x ≤ end. Return the fewest arrows.","examples":[["points = [[10, 16], [2, 8], [1, 6], [7, 12]]","2"],["points = [[1, 2], [3, 4], [5, 6], [7, 8]]","4"],["points = [[1, 2], [2, 3], [3, 4], [4, 5]]","2"]],"vizIn":"points = [[10, 16], [2, 8], [1, 6], [7, 12]]","brute":{"idea":"Try every subset of candidate arrow positions (the balloon ends) and keep the smallest that hits all.","tc":"O(n · 2ⁿ)","sc":"O(n)","code":"def find_min_arrow_shots(points):\n    xs = sorted({e for _, e in points})\n    for k in range(1, len(xs) + 1):\n        from itertools import combinations\n        for shots in combinations(xs, k):\n            if all(any(s <= x <= e for x in shots) for s, e in points):\n                return k\n    return 0","setup":""},"opt":{"idea":"Sort by end. Shoot at the first balloon's end; every balloon starting at or before that point is burst. The next unburst balloon needs a new arrow at its end.","tc":"O(n log n)","sc":"O(1)","code":"def find_min_arrow_shots(points):\n    points.sort(key=lambda p: p[1])\n    arrows, x = 0, float(\"-inf\")\n    for i, (s, e) in enumerate(points):\n        if s > x:\n            arrows += 1\n            x = e\n        else:\n            pass\n    return arrows","frames":[{"m":"Balloon [1,6] not hit → new arrow at 6","l":6,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"sorted by end","v":["1-6","2-8","7-12","10-16"],"p":{"i":0},"hl":[0],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"vars","v":[["arrows","1"],["arrow_at","6"]]}]},{"m":"Balloon [2,8] already burst by the arrow at 6","l":8,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"sorted by end","v":["1-6","2-8","7-12","10-16"],"p":{"i":1},"hl":[],"ok":[1],"bad":[]},{"k":"vars","v":[["arrows","1"]]}]},{"m":"Balloon [7,12] not hit → new arrow at 12","l":6,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"sorted by end","v":["1-6","2-8","7-12","10-16"],"p":{"i":2},"hl":[2],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"vars","v":[["arrows","2"],["arrow_at","12"]]}]},{"m":"Balloon [10,16] already burst by the arrow at 12","l":8,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"sorted by end","v":["1-6","2-8","7-12","10-16"],"p":{"i":3},"hl":[],"ok":[3],"bad":[]},{"k":"vars","v":[["arrows","2"]]}]},{"m":"Result: 2","l":-1,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"sorted by end","v":["1-6","2-8","7-12","10-16"],"p":{"i":3},"hl":[],"ok":[3],"bad":[]},{"k":"vars","v":[["arrows","2"]]}]}],"setup":""},"tests":3,"ide":{"name":"find_min_arrow_shots","stub":"def find_min_arrow_shots(points):\n    \"\"\"\n    Each balloon spans [x_start, x_end]. An arrow at x bursts every balloon with\n    start ≤ x ≤ end. Return the fewest arrows.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Write your code here\n    pass\n","usage":"print(find_min_arrow_shots([[10, 16], [2, 8], [1, 6], [7, 12]]))","tests":[{"args":"([[10, 16], [2, 8], [1, 6], [7, 12]],)","want":"2"},{"args":"([[1, 2], [3, 4], [5, 6], [7, 8]],)","want":"4"},{"args":"([[1, 2], [2, 3], [3, 4], [4, 5]],)","want":"2"}],"listify":false,"design":false,"plain":false}},"partition-labels":{"statement":"Split <code>s</code> into as many parts as possible so each letter appears in at most one part. Return the part sizes.","examples":[["s = 'ababcbacadefegdehijhklij'","[9, 7, 8]"],["s = 'eccbbbbdec'","[10]"]],"vizIn":"s = 'abacdcbef'","brute":{"idea":"For each cut position, check that no letter appears on both sides; cut wherever it's safe.","tc":"O(n²)","sc":"O(σ)","code":"def partition_labels(s):\n    sizes, start = [], 0\n    for i in range(len(s)):\n        if not set(s[start:i + 1]) & set(s[i + 1:]):\n            sizes.append(i - start + 1)\n            start = i + 1\n    return sizes","setup":""},"opt":{"idea":"Record each letter's last index. Walk s extending the current part's end to the last index of every letter seen; when i reaches the end, cut.","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(σ)","code":"def partition_labels(s):\n    last = {ch: i for i, ch in enumerate(s)}\n    sizes, start, end = [], 0, 0\n    for i, ch in enumerate(s):\n        end = max(end, last[ch])\n        if i == end:\n            sizes.append(end - start + 1)\n            start = i + 1\n    return sizes","frames":[{"m":"'a' last appears at 2 → this part ends at least at 2","l":4,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"s","v":["a","b","a","c","d","c","b","e","f"],"p":{"start":0,"i":0,"end":2},"hl":[0,1,2],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"sizes","v":[],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]}]},{"m":"'b' last appears at 6 → this part ends at least at 6","l":4,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"s","v":["a","b","a","c","d","c","b","e","f"],"p":{"start":0,"i":1,"end":6},"hl":[0,1,2,3,4,5,6],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"sizes","v":[],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]}]},{"m":"'a' last appears at 2 → this part ends at least at 6","l":4,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"s","v":["a","b","a","c","d","c","b","e","f"],"p":{"start":0,"i":2,"end":6},"hl":[0,1,2,3,4,5,6],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"sizes","v":[],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]}]},{"m":"'c' last appears at 5 → this part ends at least at 6","l":4,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"s","v":["a","b","a","c","d","c","b","e","f"],"p":{"start":0,"i":3,"end":6},"hl":[0,1,2,3,4,5,6],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"sizes","v":[],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]}]},{"m":"'d' last appears at 4 → this part ends at least at 6","l":4,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"s","v":["a","b","a","c","d","c","b","e","f"],"p":{"start":0,"i":4,"end":6},"hl":[0,1,2,3,4,5,6],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"sizes","v":[],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]}]},{"m":"'c' last appears at 5 → this part ends at least at 6","l":4,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"s","v":["a","b","a","c","d","c","b","e","f"],"p":{"start":0,"i":5,"end":6},"hl":[0,1,2,3,4,5,6],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"sizes","v":[],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]}]},{"m":"'b' last appears at 6 → this part ends at least at 6","l":4,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"s","v":["a","b","a","c","d","c","b","e","f"],"p":{"start":0,"i":6,"end":6},"hl":[0,1,2,3,4,5,6],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"sizes","v":[],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]}]},{"m":"'e' last appears at 7 → this part ends at least at 7","l":4,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"s","v":["a","b","a","c","d","c","b","e","f"],"p":{"start":7,"i":7,"end":7},"hl":[7],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"sizes","v":["7"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]}]},{"m":"'f' last appears at 8 → this part ends at least at 8","l":4,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"s","v":["a","b","a","c","d","c","b","e","f"],"p":{"start":8,"i":8,"end":8},"hl":[8],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"sizes","v":["7","1"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]}]},{"m":"Result: [7, 1, 1]","l":-1,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"s","v":["a","b","a","c","d","c","b","e","f"],"p":{"start":8,"i":8,"end":8},"hl":[8],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"sizes","v":["7","1"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]}]}],"setup":""},"tests":2,"ide":{"name":"partition_labels","stub":"def partition_labels(s):\n    \"\"\"\n    Split s into as many parts as possible so each letter appears in at most one\n    part. Return the part sizes.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Write your code here\n    pass\n","usage":"print(partition_labels('abacdcbef'))","tests":[{"args":"('ababcbacadefegdehijhklij',)","want":"[9, 7, 8]"},{"args":"('eccbbbbdec',)","want":"[10]"}],"listify":false,"design":false,"plain":false}},"assign-cookies":{"statement":"Child i is content with a cookie of size ≥ <code>g[i]</code>. Each child gets at most one cookie. Maximise the content children.","examples":[["g = [1, 2, 3], s = [1, 1]","1"],["g = [1, 2], s = [1, 2, 3]","2"]],"vizIn":"g = [1, 2, 3, 4], s = [1, 2, 2, 5]","brute":{"idea":"For each child, scan every unused cookie for the smallest that fits.","tc":"O(n · m)","sc":"O(m)","code":"def find_content_children(g, s):\n    used, count = [False] * len(s), 0\n    for need in sorted(g):\n        best = -1\n        for j, size in enumerate(s):\n            if not used[j] and size >= need and (best < 0 or size < s[best]):\n                best = j\n        if best >= 0:\n            used[best] = True\n            count += 1\n    return count","setup":""},"opt":{"idea":"Sort children and cookies. Walk the cookies; give the current cookie to the least greedy unfed child if it fits.","tc":"O(n log n + m log m)","sc":"O(1)","code":"def find_content_children(g, s):\n    g.sort()\n    s.sort()\n    child = 0\n    for j, size in enumerate(s):\n        if child < len(g) and size >= g[child]:\n            child += 1\n    return child","frames":[{"m":"Cookie 1: children fed so far 1","l":6,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"greed (sorted)","v":["1","2","3","4"],"p":{"child":1},"hl":[],"ok":[0],"bad":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"cookies (sorted)","v":["1","2","2","5"],"p":{"j":0},"hl":[0],"ok":[],"bad":[]}]},{"m":"Cookie 2: children fed so far 2","l":6,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"greed (sorted)","v":["1","2","3","4"],"p":{"child":2},"hl":[],"ok":[0,1],"bad":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"cookies (sorted)","v":["1","2","2","5"],"p":{"j":1},"hl":[1],"ok":[],"bad":[]}]},{"m":"Cookie 2: children fed so far 2","l":6,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"greed (sorted)","v":["1","2","3","4"],"p":{"child":2},"hl":[],"ok":[0,1],"bad":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"cookies (sorted)","v":["1","2","2","5"],"p":{"j":2},"hl":[2],"ok":[],"bad":[]}]},{"m":"Cookie 5: children fed so far 3","l":6,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"greed (sorted)","v":["1","2","3","4"],"p":{"child":3},"hl":[],"ok":[0,1,2],"bad":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"cookies (sorted)","v":["1","2","2","5"],"p":{"j":3},"hl":[3],"ok":[],"bad":[]}]},{"m":"Result: 3","l":-1,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"greed (sorted)","v":["1","2","3","4"],"p":{"child":3},"hl":[],"ok":[0,1,2],"bad":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"cookies (sorted)","v":["1","2","2","5"],"p":{"j":3},"hl":[3],"ok":[],"bad":[]}]}],"setup":""},"tests":2,"ide":{"name":"find_content_children","stub":"def find_content_children(g, s):\n    \"\"\"\n    Child i is content with a cookie of size ≥ g[i]. Each child gets at most one\n    cookie. Maximise the content children.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Write your code here\n    pass\n","usage":"print(find_content_children([1, 2, 3, 4], [1, 2, 2, 5]))","tests":[{"args":"([1, 2, 3], [1, 1])","want":"1"},{"args":"([1, 2], [1, 2, 3])","want":"2"}],"listify":false,"design":false,"plain":false}},"lemonade-change":{"statement":"Lemonade costs 5. Customers pay with 5, 10 or 20 in order. Starting with no money, can you give everyone correct change?","examples":[["bills = [5, 5, 5, 10, 20]","True"],["bills = [5, 5, 10, 10, 20]","False"]],"vizIn":"bills = [5, 5, 5, 10, 20]","brute":{"idea":"Try every way to make change from the bills you hold (search).","tc":"O(2ⁿ) worst","sc":"O(n)","code":"def lemonade_change(bills):\n    def go(i, fives, tens):\n        if i == len(bills):\n            return True\n        b = bills[i]\n        if b == 5:\n            return go(i + 1, fives + 1, tens)\n        if b == 10:\n            return fives > 0 and go(i + 1, fives - 1, tens + 1)\n        return (tens > 0 and fives > 0 and go(i + 1, fives - 1, tens - 1)) or (fives >= 3 and go(i + 1, fives - 3, tens))\n    return go(0, 0, 0)","setup":""},"opt":{"idea":"Count 5s and 10s. For 20, prefer 10 + 5 (keeps more 5s, which are needed for every change) and fall back to 5 + 5 + 5.","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(1)","code":"def lemonade_change(bills):\n    fives = tens = 0\n    for i, b in enumerate(bills):\n        if b == 5:\n            fives += 1\n        elif b == 10:\n            fives, tens = fives - 1, tens + 1\n        elif tens:\n            fives, tens = fives - 1, tens - 1\n        else:\n            fives -= 3\n        if fives < 0:\n            return False\n    return True","frames":[{"m":"Customer pays 5","l":10,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"bills","v":["5","5","5","10","20"],"p":{"i":0},"hl":[0],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"vars","v":[["fives","1"],["tens","0"]]}]},{"m":"Customer pays 5","l":10,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"bills","v":["5","5","5","10","20"],"p":{"i":1},"hl":[1],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"vars","v":[["fives","2"],["tens","0"]]}]},{"m":"Customer pays 5","l":10,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"bills","v":["5","5","5","10","20"],"p":{"i":2},"hl":[2],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"vars","v":[["fives","3"],["tens","0"]]}]},{"m":"Customer pays 10","l":10,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"bills","v":["5","5","5","10","20"],"p":{"i":3},"hl":[3],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"vars","v":[["fives","2"],["tens","1"]]}]},{"m":"Customer pays 20","l":10,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"bills","v":["5","5","5","10","20"],"p":{"i":4},"hl":[4],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"vars","v":[["fives","1"],["tens","0"]]}]},{"m":"Result: True","l":-1,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"bills","v":["5","5","5","10","20"],"p":{"i":4},"hl":[4],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"vars","v":[["fives","1"],["tens","0"]]}]}],"setup":""},"tests":2,"ide":{"name":"lemonade_change","stub":"def lemonade_change(bills):\n    \"\"\"\n    Lemonade costs 5. Customers pay with 5, 10 or 20 in order. Starting with no\n    money, can you give everyone correct change?\n    \"\"\"\n    # Write your code here\n    pass\n","usage":"print(lemonade_change([5, 5, 5, 10, 20]))","tests":[{"args":"([5, 5, 5, 10, 20],)","want":"True"},{"args":"([5, 5, 10, 10, 20],)","want":"False"}],"listify":false,"design":false,"plain":false}},"candy":{"statement":"Each child gets ≥ 1 candy, and a child with a higher rating than a neighbour gets more than that neighbour. Return the minimum total.","examples":[["ratings = [1, 0, 2]","5"],["ratings = [1, 2, 2]","4"]],"vizIn":"ratings = [1, 3, 4, 5, 2, 1]","brute":{"idea":"Start everyone at 1 and keep sweeping, fixing any violated neighbour, until nothing changes.","tc":"O(n²)","sc":"O(n)","code":"def candy(ratings):\n    n = len(ratings)\n    c = [1] * n\n    changed = True\n    while changed:\n        changed = False\n        for i in range(n):\n            if i > 0 and ratings[i] > ratings[i - 1] and c[i] <= c[i - 1]:\n                c[i], changed = c[i - 1] + 1, True\n            if i < n - 1 and ratings[i] > ratings[i + 1] and c[i] <= c[i + 1]:\n                c[i], changed = c[i + 1] + 1, True\n    return sum(c)","setup":""},"opt":{"idea":"Left → right: if rating rises, candy = left + 1. Right → left: if rating rises toward the left, candy = max(candy, right + 1). Both rules then hold.","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(n)","code":"def candy(ratings):\n    n = len(ratings)\n    c = [1] * n\n    for i in range(1, n):\n        if ratings[i] > ratings[i - 1]:\n            c[i] = c[i - 1] + 1\n    for i in range(n - 2, -1, -1):\n        if ratings[i] > ratings[i + 1]:\n            c[i] = max(c[i], c[i + 1] + 1)\n    return sum(c)","frames":[{"m":"Pass 1 (left → right): beat your left neighbour","l":5,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"ratings","v":["1","3","4","5","2","1"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"candy","v":["1","2","3","4","1","1"],"p":{},"hl":[0,1,2,3,4,5],"ok":[],"bad":[]}]},{"m":"Pass 2 (right → left): beat your right neighbour too. Total 13","l":8,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"ratings","v":["1","3","4","5","2","1"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"candy","v":["1","2","3","4","2","1"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[0,1,2,3,4,5],"bad":[]}]},{"m":"Result: 13","l":-1,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"ratings","v":["1","3","4","5","2","1"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"candy","v":["1","2","3","4","2","1"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[0,1,2,3,4,5],"bad":[]}]}],"setup":""},"tests":2,"ide":{"name":"candy","stub":"def candy(ratings):\n    \"\"\"\n    Each child gets ≥ 1 candy, and a child with a higher rating than a neighbour\n    gets more than that neighbour. Return the minimum total.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Write your code here\n    pass\n","usage":"print(candy([1, 3, 4, 5, 2, 1]))","tests":[{"args":"([1, 0, 2],)","want":"5"},{"args":"([1, 2, 2],)","want":"4"}],"listify":false,"design":false,"plain":false}},"valid-parenthesis-string":{"statement":"'*' can be '(' or ')' or empty. Is the string a valid parenthesis string?","examples":[["s = '()'","True"],["s = '(*)'","True"],["s = '(*))'","True"]],"vizIn":"s = '(*))(*'","brute":{"idea":"Try all three meanings of every '*'.","tc":"O(3ⁿ)","sc":"O(n)","code":"def check_valid_string(s):\n    def go(i, open_):\n        if open_ < 0:\n            return False\n        if i == len(s):\n            return open_ == 0\n        if s[i] == \"(\":\n            return go(i + 1, open_ + 1)\n        if s[i] == \")\":\n            return go(i + 1, open_ - 1)\n        return go(i + 1, open_ + 1) or go(i + 1, open_ - 1) or go(i + 1, open_)\n    return go(0, 0)","setup":""},"opt":{"idea":"Track the range [lo, hi] of possible open-bracket counts. '(' raises both, ')' lowers both, '*' lowers lo and raises hi. If hi &lt; 0 fail; clamp lo at 0; valid if lo == 0 at the end.","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(1)","code":"def check_valid_string(s):\n    lo = hi = 0\n    for i, ch in enumerate(s):\n        if ch == \"(\":\n            lo, hi = lo + 1, hi + 1\n        elif ch == \")\":\n            lo, hi = lo - 1, hi - 1\n        else:\n            lo, hi = lo - 1, hi + 1\n        if hi < 0:\n            return False\n        lo = max(lo, 0)\n    return lo == 0","frames":[{"m":"'(': open count could be anywhere in [1, 1]","l":8,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"s","v":["(","*",")",")","(","*"],"p":{"i":0},"hl":[0],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"vars","v":[["lo","1"],["hi","1"]]}]},{"m":"'*': open count could be anywhere in [0, 2]","l":8,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"s","v":["(","*",")",")","(","*"],"p":{"i":1},"hl":[1],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"vars","v":[["lo","0"],["hi","2"]]}]},{"m":"')': open count could be anywhere in [0, 1]","l":8,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"s","v":["(","*",")",")","(","*"],"p":{"i":2},"hl":[2],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"vars","v":[["lo","0"],["hi","1"]]}]},{"m":"')': open count could be anywhere in [0, 0]","l":8,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"s","v":["(","*",")",")","(","*"],"p":{"i":3},"hl":[3],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"vars","v":[["lo","0"],["hi","0"]]}]},{"m":"'(': open count could be anywhere in [1, 1]","l":8,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"s","v":["(","*",")",")","(","*"],"p":{"i":4},"hl":[4],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"vars","v":[["lo","1"],["hi","1"]]}]},{"m":"'*': open count could be anywhere in [0, 2]","l":8,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"s","v":["(","*",")",")","(","*"],"p":{"i":5},"hl":[5],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"vars","v":[["lo","0"],["hi","2"]]}]},{"m":"Result: True","l":-1,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"s","v":["(","*",")",")","(","*"],"p":{"i":5},"hl":[5],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"vars","v":[["lo","0"],["hi","2"]]}]}],"setup":""},"tests":4,"ide":{"name":"check_valid_string","stub":"def check_valid_string(s):\n    \"\"\"\n    '*' can be '(' or ')' or empty. Is the string a valid parenthesis string?\n    \"\"\"\n    # Write your code here\n    pass\n","usage":"print(check_valid_string('(*))(*'))","tests":[{"args":"('()',)","want":"True"},{"args":"('(*)',)","want":"True"},{"args":"('(*))',)","want":"True"},{"args":"(')*(',)","want":"False"}],"listify":false,"design":false,"plain":false}},"best-time-to-buy-and-sell-stock-ii":{"statement":"You may trade any number of times (hold at most one share). Maximise profit.","examples":[["prices = [7, 1, 5, 3, 6, 4]","7"],["prices = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]","4"],["prices = [7, 6, 4, 3, 1]","0"]],"vizIn":"prices = [7, 1, 5, 3, 6, 4]","brute":{"idea":"Recurse on (day, holding) trying buy, sell or wait.","tc":"O(2ⁿ)","sc":"O(n)","code":"def max_profit_ii(prices):\n    def go(i, holding):\n        if i == len(prices):\n            return 0\n        wait = go(i + 1, holding)\n        if holding:\n            return max(wait, prices[i] + go(i + 1, False))\n        return max(wait, -prices[i] + go(i + 1, True))\n    return go(0, False)","setup":""},"opt":{"idea":"Any profitable trade is a sum of day-to-day rises, so add every positive difference prices[i] − prices[i − 1].","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(1)","code":"def max_profit_ii(prices):\n    profit = 0\n    for i in range(1, len(prices)):\n        gain = prices[i] - prices[i - 1]\n        if gain > 0:\n            profit += gain\n    return profit","frames":[{"m":"Day 0 → 1: change -6","l":5,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"prices","v":["7","1","5","3","6","4"],"p":{"i":1},"hl":[0,1],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"vars","v":[["profit","0"]]}]},{"m":"Day 1 → 2: change +4 (take it)","l":5,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"prices","v":["7","1","5","3","6","4"],"p":{"i":2},"hl":[],"ok":[1,2],"bad":[]},{"k":"vars","v":[["profit","4"]]}]},{"m":"Day 2 → 3: change -2","l":5,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"prices","v":["7","1","5","3","6","4"],"p":{"i":3},"hl":[2,3],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"vars","v":[["profit","4"]]}]},{"m":"Day 3 → 4: change +3 (take it)","l":5,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"prices","v":["7","1","5","3","6","4"],"p":{"i":4},"hl":[],"ok":[3,4],"bad":[]},{"k":"vars","v":[["profit","7"]]}]},{"m":"Day 4 → 5: change -2","l":5,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"prices","v":["7","1","5","3","6","4"],"p":{"i":5},"hl":[4,5],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"vars","v":[["profit","7"]]}]},{"m":"Result: 7","l":-1,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"prices","v":["7","1","5","3","6","4"],"p":{"i":5},"hl":[4,5],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"vars","v":[["profit","7"]]}]}],"setup":""},"tests":3,"ide":{"name":"max_profit_ii","stub":"def max_profit_ii(prices):\n    \"\"\"\n    You may trade any number of times (hold at most one share). Maximise profit.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Write your code here\n    pass\n","usage":"print(max_profit_ii([7, 1, 5, 3, 6, 4]))","tests":[{"args":"([7, 1, 5, 3, 6, 4],)","want":"7"},{"args":"([1, 2, 3, 4, 5],)","want":"4"},{"args":"([7, 6, 4, 3, 1],)","want":"0"}],"listify":false,"design":false,"plain":false}},"largest-number":{"statement":"Arrange non-negative integers to form the largest number; return it as a string.","examples":[["nums = [10, 2]","'210'"],["nums = [3, 30, 34, 5, 9]","'9534330'"],["nums = [0, 0]","'0'"]],"vizIn":"nums = [10, 2]","brute":{"idea":"Try every permutation and keep the largest concatenation.","tc":"O(n! · n)","sc":"O(n)","code":"def largest_number(nums):\n    from itertools import permutations\n    best = max(\"\".join(p) for p in permutations(map(str, nums)))\n    return \"0\" if best[0] == \"0\" else best","setup":""},"opt":{"idea":"Sort with the rule: a goes before b if a + b &gt; b + a as strings. This order is transitive, and it gives the largest number. Handle all zeros.","tc":"O(n log n · k)","sc":"O(n)","code":"def largest_number(nums):\n    from functools import cmp_to_key\n    strs = [str(x) for x in nums]\n    strs.sort(key=cmp_to_key(lambda a, b: -1 if a + b > b + a else (1 if a + b < b + a else 0)))\n    res = \"\".join(strs)\n    return \"0\" if res[0] == \"0\" else res","frames":[{"m":"Compare pairs by which concatenation is bigger","l":3,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"as strings","v":["10","2"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]}]},{"m":"Sorted: ['2', '10']","l":3,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"sorted","v":["2","10"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[0,1],"bad":[]}]},{"m":"Result: '210'","l":-1,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"sorted","v":["2","10"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[0,1],"bad":[]}]}],"setup":""},"tests":3,"ide":{"name":"largest_number","stub":"def largest_number(nums):\n    \"\"\"\n    Arrange non-negative integers to form the largest number; return it as a\n    string.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Write your code here\n    pass\n","usage":"print(largest_number([10, 2]))","tests":[{"args":"([10, 2],)","want":"'210'"},{"args":"([3, 30, 34, 5, 9],)","want":"'9534330'"},{"args":"([0, 0],)","want":"'0'"}],"listify":false,"design":false,"plain":false}},"queue-reconstruction-by-height":{"statement":"Each person is [h, k]: height h with exactly k people in front who are at least as tall. Rebuild the queue.","examples":[["people = [[7, 0], [4, 4], [7, 1], [5, 0], [6, 1], [5, 2]]","[[5, 0], [7, 0], [5, 2], [6, 1], [4, 4], [7, 1]]"],["people = [[6, 0], [5, 0], [4, 0], [3, 2], [2, 2], [1, 4]]","[[4, 0], [5, 0], [2, 2], [3, 2], [1, 4], [6, 0]]"]],"vizIn":"people = [[7, 0], [4, 4], [7, 1], [5, 0], [6, 1], [5, 2]]","brute":{"idea":"Try every ordering and check each person's k.","tc":"O(n! · n²)","sc":"O(n)","code":"def reconstruct_queue(people):\n    from itertools import permutations\n    for p in permutations(people):\n        if all(sum(1 for j in range(i) if p[j][0] >= h) == k for i, (h, k) in enumerate(p)):\n            return [list(x) for x in p]","setup":""},"opt":{"idea":"Sort by height descending, k ascending. Insert each person at index k: everyone already placed is at least as tall, and shorter people added later don't change their counts.","tc":"O(n²)","sc":"O(n)","code":"def reconstruct_queue(people):\n    people.sort(key=lambda p: (-p[0], p[1]))\n    queue = []\n    for h, k in people:\n        queue.insert(k, [h, k])\n    return queue","frames":[{"m":"Insert [7,0] at index 0","l":4,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"queue","v":["7-0"],"p":{},"hl":[0],"ok":[],"bad":[]}]},{"m":"Insert [7,1] at index 1","l":4,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"queue","v":["7-0","7-1"],"p":{},"hl":[1],"ok":[],"bad":[]}]},{"m":"Insert [6,1] at index 1","l":4,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"queue","v":["7-0","6-1","7-1"],"p":{},"hl":[1],"ok":[],"bad":[]}]},{"m":"Insert [5,0] at index 0","l":4,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"queue","v":["5-0","7-0","6-1","7-1"],"p":{},"hl":[0],"ok":[],"bad":[]}]},{"m":"Insert [5,2] at index 2","l":4,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"queue","v":["5-0","7-0","5-2","6-1","7-1"],"p":{},"hl":[2],"ok":[],"bad":[]}]},{"m":"Insert [4,4] at index 4","l":4,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"queue","v":["5-0","7-0","5-2","6-1","4-4","7-1"],"p":{},"hl":[4],"ok":[],"bad":[]}]},{"m":"Result: [[5, 0], [7, 0], [5, 2], [6, 1], [4, 4], [7, 1]]","l":-1,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"queue","v":["5-0","7-0","5-2","6-1","4-4","7-1"],"p":{},"hl":[4],"ok":[],"bad":[]}]}],"setup":""},"tests":2,"ide":{"name":"reconstruct_queue","stub":"def reconstruct_queue(people):\n    \"\"\"\n    Each person is [h, k]: height h with exactly k people in front who are at\n    least as tall. Rebuild the queue.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Write your code here\n    pass\n","usage":"print(reconstruct_queue([[7, 0], [4, 4], [7, 1], [5, 0], [6, 1], [5, 2]]))","tests":[{"args":"([[7, 0], [4, 4], [7, 1], [5, 0], [6, 1], [5, 2]],)","want":"[[5, 0], [7, 0], [5, 2], [6, 1], [4, 4], [7, 1]]"},{"args":"([[6, 0], [5, 0], [4, 0], [3, 2], [2, 2], [1, 4]],)","want":"[[4, 0], [5, 0], [2, 2], [3, 2], [1, 4], [6, 0]]"}],"listify":false,"design":false,"plain":false}},"interval-list-intersections":{"statement":"Two lists of disjoint, sorted closed intervals. Return their intersection.","examples":[["first = [[0, 2], [5, 10], [13, 23], [24, 25]], second = [[1, 5], [8, 12], [15, 24], [25, 26]]","[[1, 2], [5, 5], [8, 10], [15, 23], [24, 24], [25, 25]]"],["first = [[1, 3], [5, 9]], second = []","[]"]],"vizIn":"first = [[0, 2], [5, 10], [13, 23], [24, 25]], second = [[1, 5], [8, 12], [15, 24], [25, 26]]","brute":{"idea":"Intersect every interval in A with every interval in B.","tc":"O(m · n)","sc":"O(m + n)","code":"def interval_intersection(first, second):\n    res = []\n    for a, b in first:\n        for c, d in second:\n            lo, hi = max(a, c), min(b, d)\n            if lo <= hi:\n                res.append([lo, hi])\n    return sorted(res)","setup":""},"opt":{"idea":"Two pointers: the overlap of A[i] and B[j] is [max starts, min ends] if non-empty. Then advance whichever interval ends first.","tc":"O(m + n)","sc":"O(1) extra","code":"def interval_intersection(first, second):\n    i = j = 0\n    res = []\n    while i < len(first) and j < len(second):\n        lo = max(first[i][0], second[j][0])\n        hi = min(first[i][1], second[j][1])\n        if lo <= hi:\n            res.append([lo, hi])\n        if first[i][1] < second[j][1]:\n            i += 1\n        else:\n            j += 1\n    return res","frames":[{"m":"Overlap of [0, 2] and [1, 5]: [1,2]","l":7,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"A","v":["0-2","5-10","13-23","24-25"],"p":{"i":0},"hl":[0],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"B","v":["1-5","8-12","15-24","25-26"],"p":{"j":0},"hl":[0],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"result","v":["1-2"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]}]},{"m":"Overlap of [5, 10] and [1, 5]: [5,5]","l":7,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"A","v":["0-2","5-10","13-23","24-25"],"p":{"i":1},"hl":[1],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"B","v":["1-5","8-12","15-24","25-26"],"p":{"j":0},"hl":[0],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"result","v":["1-2","5-5"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]}]},{"m":"Overlap of [5, 10] and [8, 12]: [8,10]","l":7,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"A","v":["0-2","5-10","13-23","24-25"],"p":{"i":1},"hl":[1],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"B","v":["1-5","8-12","15-24","25-26"],"p":{"j":1},"hl":[1],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"result","v":["1-2","5-5","8-10"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]}]},{"m":"Overlap of [13, 23] and [8, 12]: none","l":7,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"A","v":["0-2","5-10","13-23","24-25"],"p":{"i":2},"hl":[2],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"B","v":["1-5","8-12","15-24","25-26"],"p":{"j":1},"hl":[1],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"result","v":["1-2","5-5","8-10"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]}]},{"m":"Overlap of [13, 23] and [15, 24]: [15,23]","l":7,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"A","v":["0-2","5-10","13-23","24-25"],"p":{"i":2},"hl":[2],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"B","v":["1-5","8-12","15-24","25-26"],"p":{"j":2},"hl":[2],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"result","v":["1-2","5-5","8-10","15-23"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]}]},{"m":"Overlap of [24, 25] and [15, 24]: [24,24]","l":7,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"A","v":["0-2","5-10","13-23","24-25"],"p":{"i":3},"hl":[3],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"B","v":["1-5","8-12","15-24","25-26"],"p":{"j":2},"hl":[2],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"result","v":["1-2","5-5","8-10","15-23","24-24"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]}]},{"m":"Overlap of [24, 25] and [25, 26]: [25,25]","l":7,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"A","v":["0-2","5-10","13-23","24-25"],"p":{"i":3},"hl":[3],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"B","v":["1-5","8-12","15-24","25-26"],"p":{"j":3},"hl":[3],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"result","v":["1-2","5-5","8-10","15-23","24-24","25-25"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]}]},{"m":"Result: [[1, 2], [5, 5], [8, 10], [15, 23], [24, 24], [25, 25]]","l":-1,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"A","v":["0-2","5-10","13-23","24-25"],"p":{"i":3},"hl":[3],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"B","v":["1-5","8-12","15-24","25-26"],"p":{"j":3},"hl":[3],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"result","v":["1-2","5-5","8-10","15-23","24-24","25-25"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]}]}],"setup":""},"tests":2,"ide":{"name":"interval_intersection","stub":"def interval_intersection(first, second):\n    \"\"\"\n    Two lists of disjoint, sorted closed intervals. Return their intersection.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Write your code here\n    pass\n","usage":"print(interval_intersection([[0, 2], [5, 10], [13, 23], [24, 25]], [[1, 5], [8, 12], [15, 24], [25, 26]]))","tests":[{"args":"([[0, 2], [5, 10], [13, 23], [24, 25]], [[1, 5], [8, 12], [15, 24], [25, 26]])","want":"[[1, 2], [5, 5], [8, 10], [15, 23], [24, 24], [25, 25]]"},{"args":"([[1, 3], [5, 9]], [])","want":"[]"}],"listify":false,"design":false,"plain":false}},"two-city-scheduling":{"statement":"2n people; <code>costs[i] = [toA, toB]</code>. Send exactly n to each city at minimum total cost.","examples":[["costs = [[10, 20], [30, 200], [400, 50], [30, 20]]","110"],["costs = [[259, 770], [448, 54], [926, 667], [184, 139], [840, 118], [577, 469]]","1859"]],"vizIn":"costs = [[10, 20], [30, 200], [400, 50], [30, 20]]","brute":{"idea":"Try every way to choose n people for city A.","tc":"O(C(2n, n) · n)","sc":"O(n)","code":"def two_city_sched_cost(costs):\n    from itertools import combinations\n    n = len(costs) // 2\n    best = float(\"inf\")\n    for group in combinations(range(2 * n), n):\n        g = set(group)\n        best = min(best, sum(costs[i][0] if i in g else costs[i][1] for i in range(2 * n)))\n    return best","setup":""},"opt":{"idea":"Sort by toA − toB. The first n (who save the most by going to A) go to A, the rest to B.","tc":"O(n log n)","sc":"O(1)","code":"def two_city_sched_cost(costs):\n    costs.sort(key=lambda c: c[0] - c[1])\n    n = len(costs) // 2\n    total = sum(a for a, _ in costs[:n]) + sum(b for _, b in costs[n:])\n    return total","frames":[{"m":"Sorted by (toA − toB): first half fly to A, second half to B","l":4,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"costs [A, B]","v":["30,200","10,20","30,20","400,50"],"p":{},"hl":[2,3],"ok":[0,1],"bad":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"toA − toB","v":["-170","-10","10","350"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"vars","v":[["total","110"]]}]},{"m":"Result: 110","l":-1,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"costs [A, B]","v":["30,200","10,20","30,20","400,50"],"p":{},"hl":[2,3],"ok":[0,1],"bad":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"toA − toB","v":["-170","-10","10","350"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"vars","v":[["total","110"]]}]}],"setup":""},"tests":2,"ide":{"name":"two_city_sched_cost","stub":"def two_city_sched_cost(costs):\n    \"\"\"\n    2n people; costs[i] = [toA, toB]. Send exactly n to each city at minimum\n    total cost.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Write your code here\n    pass\n","usage":"print(two_city_sched_cost([[10, 20], [30, 200], [400, 50], [30, 20]]))","tests":[{"args":"([[10, 20], [30, 200], [400, 50], [30, 20]],)","want":"110"},{"args":"([[259, 770], [448, 54], [926, 667], [184, 139], [840, 118], [577, 469]],)","want":"1859"}],"listify":false,"design":false,"plain":false}},"maximum-units-on-a-truck":{"statement":"<code>boxTypes[i] = [count, unitsPerBox]</code>. The truck holds <code>truckSize</code> boxes. Maximise total units.","examples":[["box_types = [[1, 3], [2, 2], [3, 1]], truck_size = 4","8"],["box_types = [[5, 10], [2, 5], [4, 7], [3, 9]], truck_size = 10","91"]],"vizIn":"box_types = [[1, 3], [2, 2], [3, 1]], truck_size = 4","brute":{"idea":"Load boxes one at a time, each time scanning for the type with the most units left.","tc":"O(truckSize · n)","sc":"O(1)","code":"def maximum_units(box_types, truck_size):\n    left = [list(b) for b in box_types]\n    total = 0\n    for _ in range(truck_size):\n        best = max((b for b in left if b[0] > 0), key=lambda b: b[1], default=None)\n        if not best:\n            break\n        best[0] -= 1\n        total += best[1]\n    return total","setup":""},"opt":{"idea":"Sort box types by units per box, descending, and take as many of each as fit.","tc":"O(n log n)","sc":"O(1)","code":"def maximum_units(box_types, truck_size):\n    box_types.sort(key=lambda b: -b[1])\n    total = 0\n    for i, (count, units) in enumerate(box_types):\n        take = min(count, truck_size)\n        total += take * units\n        truck_size -= take\n        if truck_size == 0:\n            break\n    return total","frames":[{"m":"Take 1 box(es) of 3 units","l":6,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"types [count, units] by units","v":["1,3","2,2","3,1"],"p":{"i":0},"hl":[0],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"vars","v":[["space_left","3"],["total","3"]]}]},{"m":"Take 2 box(es) of 2 units","l":6,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"types [count, units] by units","v":["1,3","2,2","3,1"],"p":{"i":1},"hl":[1],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"vars","v":[["space_left","1"],["total","7"]]}]},{"m":"Take 1 box(es) of 1 units","l":6,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"types [count, units] by units","v":["1,3","2,2","3,1"],"p":{"i":2},"hl":[2],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"vars","v":[["space_left","0"],["total","8"]]}]},{"m":"Result: 8","l":-1,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"types [count, units] by units","v":["1,3","2,2","3,1"],"p":{"i":2},"hl":[2],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"vars","v":[["space_left","0"],["total","8"]]}]}],"setup":""},"tests":2,"ide":{"name":"maximum_units","stub":"def maximum_units(box_types, truck_size):\n    \"\"\"\n    boxTypes[i] = [count, unitsPerBox]. The truck holds truckSize boxes.\n    Maximise total units.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Write your code here\n    pass\n","usage":"print(maximum_units([[1, 3], [2, 2], [3, 1]], 4))","tests":[{"args":"([[1, 3], [2, 2], [3, 1]], 4)","want":"8"},{"args":"([[5, 10], [2, 5], [4, 7], [3, 9]], 10)","want":"91"}],"listify":false,"design":false,"plain":false}},"remove-covered-intervals":{"statement":"Remove every interval covered by another (c ≤ a and b ≤ d). Return how many remain.","examples":[["intervals = [[1, 4], [3, 6], [2, 8]]","2"],["intervals = [[1, 4], [2, 3]]","1"]],"vizIn":"intervals = [[1, 4], [3, 6], [2, 8]]","brute":{"idea":"For each interval, check every other interval to see if it covers it.","tc":"O(n²)","sc":"O(1)","code":"def remove_covered_intervals(intervals):\n    n = len(intervals)\n    return sum(1 for i in range(n) if not any(j != i and intervals[j][0] <= intervals[i][0] and intervals[i][1] <= intervals[j][1] for j in range(n)))","setup":""},"opt":{"idea":"Sort by start ascending and, for equal starts, end descending. An interval is covered exactly when its end ≤ the largest end seen so far.","tc":"O(n log n)","sc":"O(1)","code":"def remove_covered_intervals(intervals):\n    intervals.sort(key=lambda x: (x[0], -x[1]))\n    keep, far, kept = 0, 0, []\n    for i, (s, e) in enumerate(intervals):\n        if e > far:\n            keep += 1\n            far = e\n            kept.append(i)\n    return keep","frames":[{"m":"[1,4] kept","l":7,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"sorted","v":["1-4","2-8","3-6"],"p":{"i":0},"hl":[],"ok":[0],"bad":[]},{"k":"vars","v":[["kept","1"],["max_end","4"]]}]},{"m":"[2,8] kept","l":7,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"sorted","v":["1-4","2-8","3-6"],"p":{"i":1},"hl":[],"ok":[0,1],"bad":[]},{"k":"vars","v":[["kept","2"],["max_end","8"]]}]},{"m":"[3,6] covered (end ≤ 8)","l":7,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"sorted","v":["1-4","2-8","3-6"],"p":{"i":2},"hl":[],"ok":[0,1],"bad":[2]},{"k":"vars","v":[["kept","2"],["max_end","8"]]}]},{"m":"Result: 2","l":-1,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"sorted","v":["1-4","2-8","3-6"],"p":{"i":2},"hl":[],"ok":[0,1],"bad":[2]},{"k":"vars","v":[["kept","2"],["max_end","8"]]}]}],"setup":""},"tests":2,"ide":{"name":"remove_covered_intervals","stub":"def remove_covered_intervals(intervals):\n    \"\"\"\n    Remove every interval covered by another (c ≤ a and b ≤ d). Return how many\n    remain.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Write your code here\n    pass\n","usage":"print(remove_covered_intervals([[1, 4], [3, 6], [2, 8]]))","tests":[{"args":"([[1, 4], [3, 6], [2, 8]],)","want":"2"},{"args":"([[1, 4], [2, 3]],)","want":"1"}],"listify":false,"design":false,"plain":false}},"car-pooling":{"statement":"<code>trips[i] = [passengers, from, to]</code>. The car has <code>capacity</code> seats and drives east only. Can it complete all trips?","examples":[["trips = [[2, 1, 5], [3, 3, 7]], capacity = 4","False"],["trips = [[2, 1, 5], [3, 3, 7]], capacity = 5","True"]],"vizIn":"trips = [[2, 1, 5], [3, 3, 7], [1, 5, 8]], capacity = 6","brute":{"idea":"For every kilometre, add up the passengers of every trip covering it.","tc":"O(n · D)","sc":"O(1)","code":"def car_pooling(trips, capacity):\n    end = max(t for _, _, t in trips)\n    for km in range(end):\n        if sum(p for p, f, t in trips if f <= km < t) > capacity:\n            return False\n    return True","setup":""},"opt":{"idea":"Events: +p at 'from', −p at 'to'. Sort events (drop-offs before pick-ups at the same point) and sweep the running load.","tc":"O(n log n)","sc":"O(n)","code":"def car_pooling(trips, capacity):\n    events = sorted([(f, p) for p, f, _ in trips] + [(t, -p) for p, _, t in trips])\n    load = 0\n    for i, (x, delta) in enumerate(events):\n        load += delta\n        if load > capacity:\n            return False\n    return True","frames":[{"m":"At 1: pick up 2 → load 2","l":4,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"events (place, change)","v":["1:+2","3:+3","5:-2","5:+1","7:-3","8:-1"],"p":{"i":0},"hl":[0],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"vars","v":[["load","2"],["capacity","6"]]}]},{"m":"At 3: pick up 3 → load 5","l":4,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"events (place, change)","v":["1:+2","3:+3","5:-2","5:+1","7:-3","8:-1"],"p":{"i":1},"hl":[1],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"vars","v":[["load","5"],["capacity","6"]]}]},{"m":"At 5: drop off 2 → load 3","l":4,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"events (place, change)","v":["1:+2","3:+3","5:-2","5:+1","7:-3","8:-1"],"p":{"i":2},"hl":[2],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"vars","v":[["load","3"],["capacity","6"]]}]},{"m":"At 5: pick up 1 → load 4","l":4,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"events (place, change)","v":["1:+2","3:+3","5:-2","5:+1","7:-3","8:-1"],"p":{"i":3},"hl":[3],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"vars","v":[["load","4"],["capacity","6"]]}]},{"m":"At 7: drop off 3 → load 1","l":4,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"events (place, change)","v":["1:+2","3:+3","5:-2","5:+1","7:-3","8:-1"],"p":{"i":4},"hl":[4],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"vars","v":[["load","1"],["capacity","6"]]}]},{"m":"At 8: drop off 1 → load 0","l":4,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"events (place, change)","v":["1:+2","3:+3","5:-2","5:+1","7:-3","8:-1"],"p":{"i":5},"hl":[5],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"vars","v":[["load","0"],["capacity","6"]]}]},{"m":"Result: True","l":-1,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"events (place, change)","v":["1:+2","3:+3","5:-2","5:+1","7:-3","8:-1"],"p":{"i":5},"hl":[5],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"vars","v":[["load","0"],["capacity","6"]]}]}],"setup":""},"tests":2,"ide":{"name":"car_pooling","stub":"def car_pooling(trips, capacity):\n    \"\"\"\n    trips[i] = [passengers, from, to]. The car has capacity seats and drives\n    east only. Can it complete all trips?\n    \"\"\"\n    # Write your code here\n    pass\n","usage":"print(car_pooling([[2, 1, 5], [3, 3, 7], [1, 5, 8]], 6))","tests":[{"args":"([[2, 1, 5], [3, 3, 7]], 4)","want":"False"},{"args":"([[2, 1, 5], [3, 3, 7]], 5)","want":"True"}],"listify":false,"design":false,"plain":false}}},"demo":{"code":"def merge_demo():\n    intervals = [[1, 3], [8, 10], [2, 6], [15, 18], [9, 12]]\n    intervals.sort()\n    out = [intervals[0][:]]\n    for i in range(1, len(intervals)):\n        s, e = intervals[i]\n        if s <= out[-1][1]:\n            out[-1][1] = max(out[-1][1], e)\n        else:\n            out.append([s, e])\n    return out","frames":[{"m":"Sort by start","l":3,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"intervals","v":["1-3","2-6","8-10","9-12","15-18"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]}]},{"m":"[2,6] overlaps the last block → extend it","l":7,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"intervals","v":["1-3","2-6","8-10","9-12","15-18"],"p":{"i":1},"hl":[1],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"merged","v":["1-6"],"p":{},"hl":[0],"ok":[],"bad":[]}]},{"m":"[8,10] starts after the last block ends → new block","l":9,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"intervals","v":["1-3","2-6","8-10","9-12","15-18"],"p":{"i":2},"hl":[2],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"merged","v":["1-6","8-10"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[1],"bad":[]}]},{"m":"[9,12] overlaps the last block → extend it","l":7,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"intervals","v":["1-3","2-6","8-10","9-12","15-18"],"p":{"i":3},"hl":[3],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"merged","v":["1-6","8-12"],"p":{},"hl":[1],"ok":[],"bad":[]}]},{"m":"[15,18] starts after the last block ends → new block","l":9,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"intervals","v":["1-3","2-6","8-10","9-12","15-18"],"p":{"i":4},"hl":[4],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"merged","v":["1-6","8-12","15-18"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[2],"bad":[]}]}],"title":"Merge intervals: sort by start, then extend or start a new block"},"sections":[{"h":"Definition","body":"\n<p>A <b>greedy algorithm</b> builds a solution step by step, at each step making the choice that looks <b>best at that moment</b> (the locally optimal choice), and never reconsidering earlier choices. It is correct only for problems where local optimality leads to global optimality.</p>\n<p>An <b>interval</b> is a pair [start, end]. Interval problems (merging, scheduling, covering) are among the most common uses of greedy algorithms.</p>\n"},{"h":"When greedy works","body":"\n<h4>1. Greedy-choice property</h4>\n<p>A globally optimal solution can be reached by making a locally optimal choice first. There exists some optimal solution that agrees with the greedy choice.</p>\n<h4>2. Optimal substructure</h4>\n<p>After making the greedy choice, what remains is a smaller instance of the same problem, whose optimal solution combines with the choice to give an optimal overall solution.</p>\n<h4>How to prove it</h4>\n<ul>\n<li><b>Exchange argument</b>: take any optimal solution that differs from greedy; swap in the greedy choice and show the result is no worse.</li>\n<li><b>Greedy stays ahead</b>: show after each step greedy's partial solution is at least as good as any other's.</li>\n<li><b>Counter-example search</b>: before proving, try small inputs to break the idea. If one breaks it, switch to DP.</li>\n</ul>\n"},{"h":"Classic greedy problems","body":"\n<table>\n<tr><th>Problem</th><th>Greedy rule</th><th>Time</th></tr>\n<tr><td>Activity selection / max non-overlapping intervals</td><td>pick the interval that <b>ends earliest</b></td><td>O(n log n)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Fractional knapsack</td><td>take items by highest value/weight ratio, splitting the last</td><td>O(n log n)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Huffman coding</td><td>repeatedly merge the two least frequent symbols</td><td>O(n log n)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Minimum spanning tree (Kruskal, Prim)</td><td>add the cheapest safe edge</td><td>O(E log V)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Dijkstra</td><td>finalise the closest unvisited vertex</td><td>O(E log V)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Job sequencing with deadlines</td><td>schedule highest profit first in the latest free slot</td><td>O(n log n)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Coin change (canonical coins like 1, 2, 5, 10)</td><td>take the largest coin that fits</td><td>O(amount / coin)</td></tr>\n</table>\n<p><b>Greedy fails</b> for 0/1 knapsack and for coin change with arbitrary coins (e.g. coins 1, 3, 4 and amount 6) — those need DP.</p>\n"},{"h":"Interval theory","body":"\n<p>Two intervals [a, b] and [c, d] <b>overlap</b> when <code>a ≤ d and c ≤ b</code> (use &lt; if touching endpoints don't count). Their intersection is <code>[max(a, c), min(b, d)]</code> when non-empty.</p>\n<table>\n<tr><th>Goal</th><th>Sort by</th><th>Why</th></tr>\n<tr><td>Merge overlapping intervals</td><td>start</td><td>overlaps then become adjacent in order</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Maximum non-overlapping set / minimum removals</td><td>end</td><td>finishing earliest leaves the most room (exchange argument)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Minimum points to stab all intervals</td><td>end</td><td>a point at the earliest end hits every interval that started before it</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Maximum overlap (rooms, platforms)</td><td>events (start +1, end −1)</td><td>sweep line counts active intervals</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Remove covered intervals</td><td>start asc, end desc</td><td>a covered interval has end ≤ the max end seen so far</td></tr>\n</table>\n"},{"h":"Greedy vs dynamic programming","body":"\n<table>\n<tr><th></th><th>Greedy</th><th>Dynamic programming</th></tr>\n<tr><td>Choices per step</td><td>one (the locally best)</td><td>all, keeps the best</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Reconsiders?</td><td>never</td><td>effectively yes</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Correctness</td><td>needs a proof (greedy-choice property)</td><td>follows from optimal substructure</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Speed</td><td>usually O(n log n) or O(n)</td><td>usually O(n²) or O(n · W)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Memory</td><td>O(1) extra</td><td>table of states</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Example where it's right</td><td>fractional knapsack</td><td>0/1 knapsack</td></tr>\n</table>\n"},{"h":"Advantages, disadvantages and applications","body":"\n<div class=\"two\">\n<div class=\"pro\"><h5>Advantages</h5><ul><li>Simple and fast</li><li>Little memory</li><li>Often the optimal method for scheduling and MST problems</li><li>Good approximation when exact methods are too slow</li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"con\"><h5>Disadvantages</h5><ul><li>Not always correct — needs proof</li><li>Hard to know whether it applies without experience</li><li>Can give a poor answer silently</li></ul></div>\n</div>\n<h4>Applications</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>CPU and meeting scheduling, room / platform allocation, calendar apps.</li>\n<li>Data compression (Huffman coding).</li>\n<li>Network design (minimum spanning trees), routing (Dijkstra).</li>\n<li>Making change at a cash register (canonical coin systems).</li>\n<li>Load balancing and caching policies; approximation algorithms for NP-hard problems (set cover).</li>\n</ul>\n"}],"faq":[{"q":"What is a greedy algorithm?","a":"<p>An algorithm that makes the locally optimal choice at each step without reconsidering, hoping it leads to a global optimum. It works when the problem has the greedy-choice property and optimal substructure.</p>"},{"q":"How do you prove a greedy algorithm is correct?","a":"<p>Usually by an exchange argument: show that any optimal solution can be transformed, step by step, into the greedy solution without becoming worse. Alternatively, show greedy 'stays ahead' of any other solution at every step.</p>"},{"q":"Why does activity selection sort by end time, not start time?","a":"<p>Choosing the interval that finishes earliest leaves the maximum remaining time for others. Sorting by start can pick a long early interval that blocks many short ones.</p>"},{"q":"Give an example where greedy fails.","a":"<p>Coin change with coins {1, 3, 4} and amount 6: greedy picks 4 + 1 + 1 (3 coins), but 3 + 3 (2 coins) is optimal. 0/1 knapsack by value/weight ratio also fails.</p>"},{"q":"Fractional vs 0/1 knapsack?","a":"<p>Fractional knapsack allows taking part of an item, so greedy by value/weight ratio is optimal (O(n log n)). In 0/1 knapsack items are indivisible, greedy fails, and DP (O(n · W)) is needed.</p>"},{"q":"How do you find the minimum number of meeting rooms?","a":"<p>Sort start and end times (or events) and sweep: +1 at a start, −1 at an end; the maximum running count is the answer. Equivalently, sort by start and keep a min-heap of end times.</p>"}],"prelude":"","lessons":[{"level":"Basics","title":"What greedy means, and when it fails","body":"\n<p>A <b>greedy</b> algorithm makes the choice that looks best <i>right now</i> and never goes back. It's simple and fast — but only correct for some problems.</p>\n<p>Coins <code>[1, 3, 4]</code>, amount 6. Greedy takes the biggest coin first: 4 + 1 + 1 = <b>3 coins</b>. The best answer is 3 + 3 = <b>2 coins</b>. Greedy failed, so this problem needs DP.</p>\n<p>Before trusting a greedy idea, always try to <b>break it with a small example</b>. If you can't, look for a proof (next lesson).</p>\n","practice":[],"demo":{"code":"def greedy_fail_lesson():\n    coins, amount = [4, 3, 1], 6\n    left, used = amount, []\n    for c in coins:\n        while left >= c:\n            left -= c\n            used.append(c)\n    return len(used)","frames":[{"m":"Greedy takes the largest coin that fits: 4, 2 left","l":7,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"coins (largest first)","v":["4","3","1"],"p":{},"hl":[0],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"used","v":["4"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"vars","v":[["left","2"]]}]},{"m":"Greedy takes the largest coin that fits: 1, 1 left","l":7,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"coins (largest first)","v":["4","3","1"],"p":{},"hl":[2],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"used","v":["4","1"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"vars","v":[["left","1"]]}]},{"m":"Greedy takes the largest coin that fits: 1, 0 left","l":7,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"coins (largest first)","v":["4","3","1"],"p":{},"hl":[2],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"arr","n":"used","v":["4","1","1"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"vars","v":[["left","0"]]}]},{"m":"Greedy used 3 coins, but 3 + 3 needs only 2 → greedy is wrong here","l":7,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"greedy","v":["4","1","1"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[0,1,2]},{"k":"arr","n":"optimal","v":["3","3"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[0,1],"bad":[]}]}],"call":"greedy_fail_lesson()","setup":""}},{"level":"Core","title":"Proving a greedy: the exchange argument","body":"\n<p>To show a greedy choice is safe, take <b>any</b> optimal answer and show you can swap one of its choices for the greedy choice without making it worse. Then some optimal answer agrees with greedy, step by step.</p>\n<p>Example — <b>assign cookies</b>: give the smallest cookie that satisfies the least greedy child. If an optimal answer gives that child a bigger cookie, swapping it for the smaller one never hurts anyone else.</p>\n<p>Greedy problems usually start with the right <b>sort order</b>:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Two city scheduling: by <code>costA − costB</code>.</li>\n<li>Maximum units on a truck: by units per box, high to low.</li>\n<li>Largest number: by the rule \"a before b if a + b &gt; b + a\".</li>\n<li>Queue by height: tallest first, then insert at index k.</li>\n</ul>\n","practice":["assign-cookies","two-city-scheduling","maximum-units-on-a-truck","largest-number","queue-reconstruction-by-height"]},{"level":"Core","title":"Intervals: sort, then merge","body":"\n<p>An interval is <code>[start, end]</code>. Two intervals overlap when <code>a.start &lt;= b.end</code> and <code>b.start &lt;= a.end</code>. Sorted by start, you only need to compare each interval with the last merged one:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"py\">intervals.sort()\nout = [intervals[0]]\nfor s, e in intervals[1:]:\n    if s &lt;= out[-1][1]:            # overlaps\n        out[-1][1] = max(out[-1][1], e)\n    else:\n        out.append([s, e])</code></pre>\n<p>Insert interval is the same in one pass on an already sorted list: copy the ones before, absorb the overlapping ones, copy the rest. Intersections of two sorted lists use two pointers.</p>\n","practice":["merge-intervals","insert-interval","interval-list-intersections"]},{"level":"Core","title":"Scheduling: sort by end time","body":"\n<p>\"Keep as many non-overlapping intervals as possible\" (or \"remove as few as possible\"): sort by <b>end</b> and always keep the interval that finishes first. Finishing early leaves the most room for the rest — that's the exchange argument.</p>\n<pre><code class=\"py\">intervals.sort(key=lambda x: x[1])\nend, kept = -inf, 0\nfor s, e in intervals:\n    if s &gt;= end:\n        kept += 1; end = e</code></pre>\n<p>Same idea: <b>minimum arrows</b> to burst balloons (shoot at the first end), and <b>covered intervals</b> (sort by start, longer first, track the farthest end).</p>\n<div class=\"warn\">Sorting by start gives the wrong answer here — a long early interval would block many short ones.</div>\n","practice":["non-overlapping-intervals","minimum-number-of-arrows-to-burst-balloons","remove-covered-intervals"],"demo":{"code":"def scheduling_lesson():\n    meetings = [[1, 4], [2, 3], [3, 5], [4, 7], [6, 8], [5, 9]]\n    meetings.sort(key=lambda x: x[1])\n    end, kept = float(\"-inf\"), []\n    for i, (s, e) in enumerate(meetings):\n        if s >= end:\n            kept.append(i)\n            end = e\n        else:\n            pass\n    return len(kept)","frames":[{"m":"[2,3] starts after nothing → keep it","l":7,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"sorted by end","v":["2-3","1-4","3-5","4-7","6-8","5-9"],"p":{"i":0},"hl":[0],"ok":[0],"bad":[]},{"k":"vars","v":[["kept","1"],["last_end","3"]]}]},{"m":"[1,4] overlaps the last kept meeting → skip","l":9,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"sorted by end","v":["2-3","1-4","3-5","4-7","6-8","5-9"],"p":{"i":1},"hl":[],"ok":[0],"bad":[1]},{"k":"vars","v":[["kept","1"],["last_end","3"]]}]},{"m":"[3,5] starts after the last end → keep it","l":7,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"sorted by end","v":["2-3","1-4","3-5","4-7","6-8","5-9"],"p":{"i":2},"hl":[2],"ok":[0,2],"bad":[]},{"k":"vars","v":[["kept","2"],["last_end","5"]]}]},{"m":"[4,7] overlaps the last kept meeting → skip","l":9,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"sorted by end","v":["2-3","1-4","3-5","4-7","6-8","5-9"],"p":{"i":3},"hl":[],"ok":[0,2],"bad":[3]},{"k":"vars","v":[["kept","2"],["last_end","5"]]}]},{"m":"[6,8] starts after the last end → keep it","l":7,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"sorted by end","v":["2-3","1-4","3-5","4-7","6-8","5-9"],"p":{"i":4},"hl":[4],"ok":[0,2,4],"bad":[]},{"k":"vars","v":[["kept","3"],["last_end","8"]]}]},{"m":"[5,9] overlaps the last kept meeting → skip","l":9,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"sorted by end","v":["2-3","1-4","3-5","4-7","6-8","5-9"],"p":{"i":5},"hl":[],"ok":[0,2,4],"bad":[5]},{"k":"vars","v":[["kept","3"],["last_end","8"]]}]}],"call":"scheduling_lesson()","setup":""}},{"level":"Core","title":"Reach and running balance","body":"\n<ul>\n<li><b>Jump game</b>: track the furthest index reachable so far. If you stand past it, you're stuck.</li>\n<li><b>Jump game II</b>: like BFS — the current reach window is \"reachable in k jumps\"; the furthest point from it starts the next window.</li>\n<li><b>Gas station</b>: if the tank goes negative at station i, no start between the current start and i can work — restart at i + 1.</li>\n<li><b>Valid parenthesis string</b>: keep the range [lo, hi] of possible open counts.</li>\n<li><b>Stock II</b>: add every positive day-to-day rise.</li>\n<li><b>Lemonade change</b>: give the biggest bills first to keep small ones.</li>\n</ul>\n","practice":["jump-game","jump-game-ii","gas-station","valid-parenthesis-string","best-time-to-buy-and-sell-stock-ii","lemonade-change"]},{"level":"Advanced","title":"Sweep lines and two passes","body":"\n<h4>Sweep line</h4>\n<p>Turn intervals into <b>events</b>: <code>+1</code> at a start, <code>−1</code> at an end. Sort events by time (ends before starts at the same time when touching doesn't overlap) and walk them with a running total. The peak is the max overlap — rooms needed, passengers in the car.</p>\n<h4>Two passes</h4>\n<p>When a rule involves both neighbours, satisfy one side at a time. Candy: left → right gives more than the left neighbour; right → left fixes the right neighbour while keeping the max.</p>\n<h4>Last occurrence</h4>\n<p>Partition labels: record each letter's last index; a part can end only when you reach the furthest last index of the letters inside it.</p>\n","practice":["car-pooling","candy","partition-labels"]}]};
